** MMP9400 - LABELLED STATEMENT REGRESSION FIXTURE (ISSUE #25)
** SETA./SETB./SETC. are generic labels preceding recognised verbs -- the
** label must not defeat the verb match. SETD. precedes a genuinely
** unrecognised statement, which must still raise an honest unparsed_line
** gap rather than a false-positive match.
DEFINE DATA LOCAL
1 #STATUS (A1)
END-DEFINE
SETA. MOVE 'CONF' TO #STATUS
SETB. CALLNAT 'PROGA'
SETC. IF #STATUS = 'CONF'
END-IF
SETD. FROBNICATE #STATUS
END
